   "mainaiger": {
    "example": true,
    "name": "review-chats",
    "title": "Review imported chats as a Mainbook (review, choose, keep, loop)"
   }
  },
  "cells": [
   {
    "id": "readme",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Review imported chats, as a Mainbook"
     }
    },
    "source": "# Review imported chats, as a Mainbook\n\nThe REVIEW section of the Memory page, laid out as cards. **Review next chat** is a Memory cell: the Lab takes the next unreviewed chat in `chats/` and asks your local model what is worth keeping (`proposal`; nothing is written). **Choose items** is plain Python — the rule for what to keep (edit it: keep only facts and procedures, require a minimum length, drop items whose title repeats a note you have, or `raise SystemExit` to stop and look). **Keep** writes the chosen items as *draft* notes linked to the chat and marks the chat reviewed — it only runs when the arrow's condition holds (a real chat, and the model answered). **Report** prints what happened, and its loop arrow goes back to **Review next chat** while chats are pending, at most 3 more per run. Needs a running session, an approved Memory folder with imported chats, and an installed model. Drafts stay drafts until you mark them stable on the Memory page.\n",
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "review",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Review next chat",
      "memory": {
       "op": "review",
       "output": "proposal"
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "choose",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Choose items"
     }
    },
    "source": "# The rule for what to keep from each chat. Plain Python over `proposal`; edit freely.\nWANTED = (\"fact\", \"procedure\", \"rule\", \"preference\")\npath = proposal[\"chat\"][\"path\"] if proposal[\"chat\"] else None\nmodel = proposal[\"model\"]\nitems = [i for i in proposal[\"items\"] if i[\"kind\"] in WANTED and len(i[\"text\"]) >= 20]\nif path is None:\n    print(\"nothing left to review\")\nelse:\n    print(\"chat:\", proposal[\"chat\"][\"title\"], \"| %d proposed, keeping %d | %d chat(s) still pending\" % (len(proposal[\"items\"]), len(items), proposal[\"pending\"]))\n    for i in items:\n        print(\" +\", i[\"title\"], \"(%s)\" % i[\"kind\"])\n    if proposal[\"error\"]:\n        print(\"model problem, nothing will be kept:\", proposal[\"error\"])\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "keep",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Keep",
      "memory": {
       "op": "keep",
       "output": "kept"
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "report",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Report"
     }
    },
    "source": "print(\"kept %d draft note(s) from %s; %d chat(s) still pending\" % (len(kept[\"written\"]), kept[\"chat\"], kept[\"review\"][\"pending\"]))\nfor w in kept[\"written\"]:\n    print(\" -\", w[\"path\"])\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   }
  ]
 },
